    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A \"Progressive\" view is one that actively seeks to modernize society, challenge outdated power structures, and expand rights for marginalized groups. Conversely, a \"Regressive\" view is one that seeks to preserve traditional hierarchies and resist social change, often favoring the status quo of established power. To illustrate this, you can contrast movements advocating for climate action (progressive) against those demanding strict adherence to historical norms without adaptation (regressive). This framework helps students see that the labels reflect a fundamental belief in whether society should evolve or remain fixed.",
